    "answer": {
      "short": "He forgot to take the square root. $x=13\\text{ cm}$.",
      "worked": "Jayden found $x^2$, then treated it as $x$. He must take the square root of both sides.\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2&=169\\\\x&=\\sqrt{169}\\\\x&=13\\text{ cm}\\end{align*}$$",
